<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέρμερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>baneful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i>) always in neut. pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέρμερα
				μητίσασθαι</span> to devise <i>mischief</i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.48
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ῥέζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.502
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. μήσατο ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.289
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				524
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of <i>warlike deeds</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμοιο μ. ἔργα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.453
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ῥέζων</span>, of Zeus,
				<i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				21a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἔργα γυναικῶν</span> the
				<i>ills</i> that women work, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				603
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					509
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλάβη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					949
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδρανίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					248
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>captious, fastidious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hp.Ma.</u>
				290e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθνος Λατίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					350
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. χρῆμα</span>
			<i>crafty</i> creature, of a fox, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.988a
			</span></i>; of a hound, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.490
			</span></i>.— 
				Ep.
			 word, used in <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> ll. cc.</div>
